Was considering lately the ability of pudding farming and whether an
early pudding farm carries the best odds.  So ... I was actually
playing around with a trans-alignment Knight and found a sink on level
5 and decided to test my theory.

My hypothesis:
an early pudding farm carries the best odds of ascension over just
playing normally.

So to test my theory, after having found my sink I descended to
Sokoban with my pet warhorse and lucked out with a wand of lightning
on Soko2 and killed a dwarf on Mines 1 for his pickaxe.  Then I pushed
around some existing boulders to make my position a little safer and
kicked the sink.  (I realized that I should have converted the
adjacent altar _before_ getting the "You Caitiff!" messages but oh
well.

With the rations that I picked up from 1.5 levels of Sokoban but no
ring of slow digestion, it's now been 6 or 7 thousand turns of holding
down the attack key and I'm at level 14.  I was soon able to skip all
of the -more- prompts as I got a towel from a death drop.  Now I can
literally just hold down ^A and let the loot pile up!  I soon found a
lamp so I left it on to identify it as oil, but then at turn 10,500 I
zapped a wand .... "For what do you wish?" Nice ...

Getting back to my question.  What do people think.  If you found a
sink on level 1-5 and were then able to find an iron item, a scroll of
scare monster or a wand of fire or lightning, or even a ring of
levitation, would your best odds be with a pudding farm?  I realize
many people have, shall we say, strong opinions on pudding farming
related to its broken-ness but my question is more related to
ascension odds.  In my opinion the pudding farm carries far fewer
dangers with far less concentration required than pillaging and
looting the dungeon normally.  I think if I were playing just to win
it would be the way to go.

